# The land, proved by walking it. Options: --seed=7 --weather=clear:0
#   tools/tour.sh tours/landscape-polish.tour --seed=7 --weather=clear:0
# What it holds the land to: the bonelands is cracked stone and not a tiled
# floor; every ground has something to read at the zoom the game is played at;
# the moss's water is black with green edges and wears no sea foam; a village
# reads as people living in a ruin; and a crown never hides a fight.
hour 12
place bonelands
wait 2
shot 01-bonelands-pavement
zoom 6
wait 1
shot 02-bonelands-pavement-close
zoom 15
walk 1,0 3 run
wait 1
shot 03-bonelands-walked
place bonelands-burning
wait 2
shot 04-bonelands-burning-ecotone
place moss
wait 2
shot 05-moss-black-water
zoom 7
wait 1
shot 06-moss-water-close
zoom 15
village 0
wait 2
shot 07-village-noon
walk 0,1 1.2
wait 1
zoom 7
wait 1
shot 08-village-close
zoom 15
place pinewood
wait 2
shot 09-pinewood
near pine
wait 1.2
shot 10-under-the-crown
zoom 9
wait 0.6
shot 11-crown-cleared-close
zoom 15
place snowfield
wait 2
shot 12-snowfield-keeps-the-page
place burning
wait 2
shot 13-burning
hour 23
wait 1.5
shot 14-bonelands-night
